  "title": "Choreography vs Orchestration",
  "description": "Choose between choreography and orchestration for sagas.",
  "order": 4,
  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "estimatedMinutes": 18,
  "tags": ["choreography", "orchestration", "saga"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Sagas can be coordinated via choreography (each service reacts to events) or orchestration (a central coordinator directs the saga)."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Key Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "Choreography",
            "definition": "Services coordinate through events without a central coordinator."
          },
          {
            "term": "Orchestration",
            "definition": "A central coordinator directs the saga steps."
          },
          {
            "term": "Saga Orchestrator",
            "definition": "A service that manages saga execution."
          },
          {
            "term": "Event-Driven Saga",
            "definition": "A saga implemented with events (choreography)."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Choreography"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Each service listens for events",
          "No central coordinator",
          "Loose coupling",
          "Hard to see the big picture",
          "Risk of cyclic dependencies"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Orchestration"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Central orchestrator manages the saga",
          "Clear control flow",
          "Easier to monitor and debug",
          "Orchestrator can become a bottleneck",
          "Tighter coupling to orchestrator"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Comparison"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": ["Aspect", "Choreography", "Orchestration"],
        "rows": [
          ["Coordinator", "None", "Central orchestrator"],
          ["Coupling", "Loose", "Tighter"],
          ["Visibility", "Hard to trace", "Easy to trace"],
          ["Complexity", "Distributed", "Centralized"],
          ["Best For", "Simple flows", "Complex flows"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Recommendation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Use orchestration for complex sagas with many steps and clear control flow. Use choreography for simple, event-driven flows with few steps."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Architecture"
      }
    },
